          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: Around midnight, the witness observes an orange light moving silently from right to left, followed by several others at intervals of a few minutes. No other testimonies are collected. The observation of orange lights crossing the sky in a few minutes, succeeding on the same trajectory, on a weekend night, strongly suggests Thai lanterns, likely released nearby after a private party. The movement is observed towards the northeast, which is consistent with the very light, variable wind from the west to the southwest reported in Tours: weather. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\", probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
